# Translation of the Museum of Alternative Displays into Français.
# How to work on this file: TRANSLATING.md at the top of the repository.
# 
# French, as it is written in France. English is the source, and this file says the same things key for key.
# The spaces of French typography are written out as escapes so that they survive editing:   is the narrow
# no-break space that goes before a colon, a semicolon, a question mark or an exclamation mark, inside guillemets
# and between the thousands of a number.   is the no-break space between a figure and what it counts.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: Museum of Alternative Displays\n"
"Report-Msgid-Bugs-To: https://github.com/obartra/museum-of-alternative-displays/issues\n"
"Language: fr\n"
"Language-Team: Français\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=2; plural=(n > 1);\n"

